{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c46c97800626c106","type":"group","x":1460,"y":-1980,"width":1140,"height":380,"label":"Character Overviews"},
		{
			"id":"9f8b28e6eae10159",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**building a foundation before you know any better. And the disproportionate value we as a society attribute to sticking to it.**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":540,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"e7a7183d5b297ca4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Heidegger and dwelling**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":700,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4aa76be0a4ea6aa6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Nudity and the Church**\nCount Sternberg",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":780,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f2bf35a697037258",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"- Assumed authority\n- Consequent responsibility \n- Fear and Failure\n- Family",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":400,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"495ade149062d288",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Carver clementine dialogue boss battle twd s 2**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":680,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"85c61ebaf62e6f67",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Schopenhauer",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":760,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"89dee6aa8e70af46",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"It is an examination of Pascal’s wager through the lens of the ethics of care.\n\nRelational Ethics?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":800,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"e8f765f8f5ecbcd1",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Leviathanism\nalmighty force presiding over peace",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":860,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"2336e6d11253b363",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The second Sex",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":840,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"69c319a2f9c95d34",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Homeschooling -> save children from the evil secular world.\n\n“They had a plan for women, we didn’t. That’s why they’re winning”\n\nParrallel to men and Tate?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":960,
			"width":260,
			"height":240
		},
		{
			"id":"549625d9b7e3557d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"moral majority\nex: Abortion wasn’t always a contentious issue",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":980,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"1f4b4f10e255500b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\"Meet them where they are\"\n->Bikers/Skaters for Christ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":1100,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f2f49b50fe13d130",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Terrorists dwelling caves**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":1180,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"41c5a717d3e43f63",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Want to do good but can’t. Makes someone else, someone stronger do it for them. Is it their good that’s been done?\n\nI’ve created good where there was none.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":400,
			"width":260,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"dc87991df32a396f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Certainty at a cost",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":640,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"47d8404a0b853a8a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Iwabo is a game about control. And fear. The balance between acceptance and defiance. Family. Conservation.**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":720,
			"width":260,
			"height":160
		},
		{
			"id":"6e89f2a5bf8c3e73",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Themes / Questions / Philosophy",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-820,
			"y":320,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"6c22ef6813709ec7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"UX",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-760,
			"y":-500,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"6cd83b9d0d1969e0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Walls closing in, letterboxing, the lower the mood",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-700,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"30f7b4758debd41e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The main menu is a fridge with child drawings etc?\nThe fridge represents the need to conserve and coldness it takes to do what’s necessary. The family is put front and center yet feels tacked on and somewhat shallow. The food inside, over time, turns.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-700,
			"y":-340,
			"width":260,
			"height":240
		},
		{
			"id":"f8237c74da98e94b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Use marble sculpture?\n\nReligious connotation\nMisconception and idealization of a past that never was",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-700,
			"y":-80,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"7cab449332d44b05",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Go even further?\nif something major happens:\nThe father realises, the marble cracks!",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-700,
			"y":80,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"869d142a688edb7d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Is Greek tragedy\nIt’s oedipus from the perspective of the father\n\nIt’s cronos \nDevouring child-> April watching younger self consumed, Daryl huge, eyes wide open, caught in the act, afraid",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":1260,
			"width":260,
			"height":260
		},
		{
			"id":"fe86ab82480ab065",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Act I",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1740,
			"y":560,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9072b482a13764b5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"- Rent transport vans, tetris furniture\n- Multiple vans per day possible\n- If you get a driver -> iwabo (they know location)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1700,
			"y":640,
			"width":260,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"7e50a73aa905894f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"14.09.2024",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1300,
			"y":520,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4208d0d3f574f5bf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"26.06.2026",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1300,
			"y":600,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4ebaee4e4165a938",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What point is served by telling someone they have to apologise?\n\n  \n\nMany of the character driven story beats depend on Daryl’s input. But even the best advice wouldn’t be as essential in shaping them into “good” people, if they had any outside influence whatsoever.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":480,
			"width":260,
			"height":300
		},
		{
			"id":"515aed9087b74054",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"[Perspective Paintings, Religion](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/EN0PHj0P__M)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":400,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"60b7eaaaf717411f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"18.04.2025 -> checkout",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1320,
			"y":840,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"47ac10f1ef8d89d9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**How much do you need to do, and what to be a “good person”**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":1220,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"6d0b97dec1d05221",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"06.07.2025",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1300,
			"y":680,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"852b20ab6d9051b7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"06.97\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1360,
			"y":740,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2729e36c5f914380",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"B route in act 1 is seeking therapy\n\nSo essentially:  \nI want to sell the player on the impending apocalypse. Easiest way to, regardless of actual “cause” is to create a meta narrative reinforcing that belief. B route end is waking up at the beginning after facing the uncertainty, mirroring a game over screen. Time limit during the day suggests urgency to act (and could be complete bullshit). The further you fall behind on prepping, the more it seems to be on the news. A heartbeat sound somewhere in the far distance. The screen tinting to a shade of red over time. Things like that.\n\nYou alleviate these symptoms by working towards the bunker.\n\nOr, by seeking therapy.\n\nIn that case the secret end ends the world actually. Haha",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1700,
			"y":860,
			"width":260,
			"height":760
		},
		{
			"id":"06efd442755c895b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Women need to “die to themselves”\n\n“You are a help meat”\n\n“Accept gods creation order”\n\n->complementarianism",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":900,
			"width":260,
			"height":200
		},
		{
			"id":"8f14555dd4765bc3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Offer a (false) plan for an impossible situation \n\n(How to build your bunker guide)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":1120,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"613e58c0f4ee9010",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Religion is helpful bc it gives clear instructions and sense of agency/order to traumatic events?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":1200,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"89397f60e4408000",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"References",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":160,
			"y":340,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a5d047ea6d936a61",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Dumbbells\nYou’re strong and fit and the other things. True alpha.\n\nMaintaining your mass means eating more, spending time exercising and costly equipment. \n\nCan’t pay too much for beauty.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":20,
			"width":260,
			"height":260
		},
		{
			"id":"784d8b017920038a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Btb Josh Duggar",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":420,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"b4513b8fa529cc9c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Culture “war”\n\nQuiverful by [Kathryn Joyce](https://www.amazon.de/-/en/Kathryn-Joyce/e/B001JSBTGG/ref=dp_byline_cont_book_1)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":500,
			"width":260,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"5aa92fc7a84c37e3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Dice - Gambler, +1 on all checks, can see the odds?**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-60,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"fa2adbb00d164a6f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Bill Gothard\nInstitute to basic life principles",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":180,
			"y":600,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"8a8aabf36f9db1e3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Go full religion:\nDaryl turns to god and eventually is heard! The player for the first time doesn’t speak for Daryl, but to him!\n\nThis can imply two things: \n1 - you are the god who’s watching. The god outside the machine.\n2 - Or you are still Daryl, but disassociating from the self, to play your own god.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-420,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":360
		},
		{
			"id":"96cbf7201f5e4bfa",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Environment",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1160,
			"y":-500,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a385a299b8f8f8d5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Morale",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-120,
			"y":-500,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"fcff41e5e11fa2e9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Rim world mood buffs, adding up, trigger rolls.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-80,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"eef49cfa59ec1f0c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Traits",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":240,
			"y":-500,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"724fa120ebc5d20b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Make skill checks easier or harder by setting “goal “ with better or worse rewards.**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"e99e7492460264a9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Consider the groups that would wind up in the bunker, the traits between them, overlaps, differences, use that as basis for the skills/items",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-300,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"78515ed3d9826e25",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Skills:\nIntrusive thoughts",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-140,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"61be34423156b3f6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Paranoia - Foresight +\n\nActing in character rewarded different from against character (growth)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":560,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"5e9ef47ae898ce46",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Silo the only place for a tree\nOr a trash heap",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1100,
			"y":-420,
			"width":260,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"1ea7221e1bc425f4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Beauty",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":1340,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"59d84d9b1c1f4ff8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Eschatology\nStudy of last things",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":1340,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a47e2753e3d0a460",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Our politics don’t dictate how susceptible we are to propaganda",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":1420,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"01d218d1a34e4db4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**rhetorical slight of hand**\nNot always. Not even usually. But sometimes.\n\nExploration and dissection of my own flaws.\n\nResponsibilities in family matters.\n\nYou can’t put all the blame on me, you’re your own person.\n\nWhen that’s not even what’s said.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-500,
			"y":1420,
			"width":260,
			"height":360
		},
		{
			"id":"fb4218b43cd3de97",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"how much should you expect people to have the why engine running",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":1540,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"9f5a7b9a19ea1535",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"No True Scottsmen",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":1540,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"aec8bc3306ea1c31",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Trinity",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-220,
			"y":1620,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"bf3d968b3270b5a3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Gut defence mechanism (you just dont like thou because of women)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-780,
			"y":1660,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"253f0f60fbde00b9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"June disassembles something",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-620,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"49fa71902537efd9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"He takes April hunting again, she needs to learn\n\nI don’t want to kill it\n\nYou cant afford to be that person if you want to survive with us.\n\nAnd you not surviving with us is not an option.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-880,
			"width":260,
			"height":280
		},
		{
			"id":"7448ba66724fffc5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Much like Daryl spending loads of food and time on gym maxing, eventually the player notices Mary-Ann “letting herself go”. The player can accept or respect this, but also call it out. Which may lead to her becoming much less effective at everything else. Time and effort spent on looking good, that could be spent on maintenance and frankly - rest.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-560,
			"y":-940,
			"width":260,
			"height":340
		},
		{
			"id":"92603f04b85dcdaf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Mary-Ann isn’t too happy with June reading about other religions. To her they’re more curiosities rather than “serious religion”",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-280,
			"y":-780,
			"width":260,
			"height":160
		},
		{
			"id":"45623c6d89d9d0c8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"mary-ann breaks apils guitar",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-700,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4afd5ea919af9eb6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"april and june play catch and knock over the food table",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-780,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9e808b2dada093e2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Someone falls into the rising water in the silo\n\nThey swim in standing water",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-920,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"d8071d760c1bb7cf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**April goes on a journey to discover other religions**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-280,
			"y":-860,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"96df3bb6fefac1d3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**April snaps out of it by telling off Maryann for letting herself go and Mary Ann retorting she’s doing the same thing. But she does so out of a feeing of superiority, and must later uplift ma as well to redeem this.**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-280,
			"y":-1100,
			"width":260,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"058433a186414683",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Go full religion. Play baroque music preach from the pulpit that is the service stair to the second floor.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1020,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"46b9fc42fd967549",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**You’re not going to win any awards with that one**\n\nOkay? Who cares?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-560,
			"y":-1080,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"723e287c0c2b287e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"They fight over their interpretations of a book. But not over what’s right or wrong, but rather over who gets the book",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-1080,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"c834f24f09d65a50",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"June tries to carry a heavy food bucket and drops it. Do you try and scrape it back in? Accept the loss, scold her?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1160,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"533b340871aac769",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Rushing to the bunker. Heavy storm to dead of night.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-560,
			"y":-1160,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"67ac1e34c17e5e1b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**The storm is a day early**",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-1160,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"d2734bc25e601a19",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"April does the dust blow cave painting, using June as the model\n\nNaturally June is covered head to toe in dust\nYou find her, June laughing April looking ertappt\nHuge mess\n\nArt critic\n-> will notice the implication\nDo you commend the work?\nDo you shut it down?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-280,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":360
		},
		{
			"id":"c807c990547bebd8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Accidents, sickness, someone chokes on food",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-1240,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9a651d3a97ffaebc",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Runs out of Paint (starts using rations)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1240,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"5da253915011c183",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Already at the bunker?\n\nWatch the sun go down before locking yourself in.\n\nBirds flying low.\n\n  \n\nWaiting for the end? Sundown.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-560,
			"y":-1360,
			"width":260,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"649821d928f6ef1c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Tree roots growing through ceiling",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-1320,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"b1002a74d430f23a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Runs out of paper (starts painting on walls)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1320,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"e44cd969a488dac2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Why not sell the bunker?\n\nA lot of the games weight (actually not a lot, or at least not most, seeing that they will never get the years they lost back), hinges on them coming out of it with nothing, having left their house and everything behind. There are a few ways to attempt to fix this.\n\n  \n\n1 - when the attempt to sell it, the government or relatives of moneybags seize the property.\n\n  \n\n2 - selling it causes the cycle to continue. the only bidder is clearly planning to move his family there. And the characters decide against it because they dont want them to experience the same they do.\n\n  \n\n3 - they seal the bunker when they leave it\n\n  \n\n4 - they move back into the bunker, only coming out occasionally",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":0,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":540,
			"height":400
		},
		{
			"id":"e8885cff8befa1b7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Masturbatory\n\nWhat’s wrong with masturbation? As long as I don’t expect people to ooh and aah at my brilliance. Besides, plenty of women have made good bank with that sort of thing in their bedrooms, so why shouldn’t in my study?\n\nWait, what do you know about women in bedrooms?\n\nWe did have the internet didn’t we?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":0,
			"y":-1060,
			"width":260,
			"height":400
		},
		{
			"id":"38957ccd05ffcd21",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Hunting ghosts (?)\nNo matter how many books, always more outside\n\nContinuations\n\nEmergency",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1120,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"c35d16af55d4b6b6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Playing hide and seek; kid “too old”",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1400,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"3577b29cdaac3450",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The Kids talk about what they would have been, had things been different.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-560,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"1584922057b37837",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Playing hide and seek kid goes where they shouldn’t",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-840,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"533c92469780b7f5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"June loses a Tooth",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-820,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"0a0e12ce48d643c0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Mary-Ann finds her faith once more or never finds god again but finds comfort in ritual",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-740,
			"width":260,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"f7f09810e99753cb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Telling June Santa isnt real",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-900,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"579440b55f9108fb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"(Forgot) Wedding Anniversary",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-980,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a14f0d67f73461cf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Forgot Junes Birthday",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":280,
			"y":-1060,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"47c0c5e6ad288dd2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Harold, while straight, used moneybags’ being gay to his advantage. He gave up some part of his masculinity to save his son.\n\nWhy did he die in a care facility?\n\nWhere are your siblings? \n\nWhy only us?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":300
		},
		{
			"id":"dcc7933c60744547",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Kids find /play with /hurt with gun",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":560,
			"y":-1480,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2d77445876732e82",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Backstory",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1160,
			"y":-1560,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
